# Adventure Opening and Campaign Persistence Handoff

## Current objective

Joel wants the next slice to make the **opening of an adventure generative and Referee-led** before normal player play begins.

New prompt from Joel:

> it'd be interesting to add some generatve flavor to the OPENING of the adventure so the ref runs some turns picking a starting scenario for the gang
>
> also thinking about how to expand the campaign and persist it broadly

Interpretation: before the current Town Module Table drops the party into the same fixed starting frame, the Referee should run a small bounded setup procedure that chooses / composes a **TableRun opening seed** from AdventureModule material, current fronts, and player-safe starting conditions.

Joel clarified: this is **TableRun first**, not campaign bootstrap. It can be fairly small: a different opening seed so production/test runs are less same-same every reset. Joel also clarified the seed should be **model-generated**, not merely Referee-selected from a fixed authored menu, it should **definitely be allowed to start away from Mort's bar**, it should use **one party-wide starting situation** rather than split-party openings, and the **event log is canonical truth** for the committed opening. The opening seed must happen **after Session Zero / party creation**, because the Referee should pick a starting scenario for the actual gang. Future campaign persistence can later bias openings, but this slice should not require broad campaign infrastructure.

Session Zero must be real: the run should actually roll/create new unique characters every time. Do not use fixed named characters, switch-statement party templates, or table-picked canned characters as runtime behavior. Character creation receipts should be visible in the Agent Dungeon x-ray view / event log.

Approved Session Zero shape: dice/domain logic creates the real receipts first, then the model participates after rolls to choose names, quirks, bonds, personality, and why this specific gang is together. The model should not replace dice receipts or invent unrolled mechanical stats.

Do **not** build a generic VTT. Do **not** create fake fallback content. Do **not** build campaign persistence first. This should be a small runnable learning slice.

